  "detail": null,
  "summary": "The messages queue is cleared: 7 refill requests from 3 patients, all decided under the refill protocol RBC-RX-05 and closed. Three new items arrived while I worked (two new results and a lab correction). They reversed all three lisinopril refills, so those are waiting on your review. Every metformin refill went through.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027) – lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled.**\n- I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill. His August potassium of 5.9 was on a damaged (hemolyzed) sample, so it didn't count, and I ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- A St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 then arrived on a good sample with potassium 5.8. I cancelled the renewal; nothing was dispensed.\n- His old order (mr-00283) is now stopped. There is an urgent review task for you (task-t0014), and he got a corrected message.\n- The repeat BMP order is still active, but the 10/20 BMP may make it unnecessary. The task asks you to decide.\n- His hernia repair is rescheduled to 11/12.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030) – metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004).\n- His portal message and two pharmacy requests were one request, covered by this one order.\n- Basis: eGFR 58 (corrected today from 65) and HbA1c 7.1% from an outside lab on 8/19.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030) – lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled.**\n- I first renewed it, but the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49.\n- That is 35% above his 1.10 from before the 9/18 dose increase. The protocol treats a rise over 30% like a potassium of 5.5 or higher.\n- I cancelled the renewal. His old order (mr-00295) is stopped, there is an urgent review task for you (task-t0015), and he got a corrected message.\n- He says his 20 mg supply has run out.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031) – metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007).\n- Basis: eGFR 92 and HbA1c 6.9% from 9/28. A 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled sample), so I ignored it.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031) – lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled.**\n- His last BMP was more than 12 months ago, so I first gave a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP (sr-t0006).\n- A potassium of 5.8 from 10/22 then arrived. I cancelled the 30-day supply.\n- His old order (mr-00297) is stopped, there is an urgent review task for you (task-t0016), and he got a corrected message.\n- The BMP order is still active.\n\n**What's in the charts:** each patient got a reply, plus a corrected message where a decision changed. Each has a signed note recording the decisions and why they changed (doc-t0020, doc-t0021, doc-t0022).\n\n**Still open in your results queue:** I didn't clear it, since you asked only for messages. The three new items I acted on (inbox-a0001, inbox-a0002, inbox-a0004) are still there as unclosed items. So are seven older results, including critical potassiums of 6.3 for pt-0016 and 6.4 for pt-0008.",
